<properties>
    <!-- Invite build only (monkey-invite.jungle). The unlock key the tester is mailed after
         sending in the request code from the lock screen; LockGate re-validates it on every
         onSettingsChanged, so it takes effect without restarting the app. Empty = locked.
         Deliberately NOT in resources/settings/: the public app must not show a setting
         whose gate is compiled out. -->
    <property id="unlockKey" type="string"></property>

    <!-- Raw 100 Hz accelerometer into the FIT: ON everywhere else, OFF for invite testers.
         It is ~96 % of a session file — about 10 MB for two hours — and every byte of that
         crosses BLE to the phone before the activity appears in Garmin Connect. On the dev and
         beta builds that trade is worth it: the raw stream is the validation vehicle the whole
         lab pipeline is built on. An invite tester gets none of that benefit and all of the
         wait, and a tester who thinks the app is broken because the sync takes twenty minutes
         is a tester lost.

         This is a PROPERTIES override rather than a code default on purpose: on a real device
         properties.xml beats whatever AppSettings' `_bool(key, dflt)` fallback says, so a code
         branch here would ship the OLD default and nothing would notice (the same trap
         docs/plan.md records for the page table). resources-invite/ is appended to
         base.resourcePath by monkey-invite.jungle only, so this row exists in exactly one
         build and the shared resources/settings/properties.xml keeps its `true` for the rest.

         The GCM toggle itself stays in resources/settings/settings.xml for every build, so a
         tester who wants to send a session in for analysis can turn it on. And the flag gates
         only the SensorLogger: the live PumpDetector registers its own listener from
         SessionController._startAccel(), behind `pumpDetection`, and is untouched here. -->
    <property id="accelLogging" type="boolean">false</property>
</properties>
